{
  "$schema": "https://json.schemastore.org/claude-code-settings.json",
  "_comment": [
    "Engineering framework permissions floor. Copy the `permissions` object",
    "into your repository's .claude/settings.json, or let",
    "/engineering-framework:framework-install merge it for you.",
    "",
    "WHY THIS IS A FILE YOU COPY RATHER THAN SOMETHING THE PLUGIN SHIPS:",
    "a plugin's settings.json supports only the `agent` and",
    "`subagentStatusLine` keys, so a plugin cannot ship permission rules. The",
    "plugin's command guard hook covers the same operations and more forms, but",
    "a hook is executable code that can fail, and Claude Code treats a crashed",
    "hook as a non-blocking error. A deny rule cannot fail open. Install both.",
    "",
    "THE ALLOW TIER IS NOT DECORATION, IT IS THE POINT.",
    "A floor of deny and ask rules with no allow tier makes nobody safer. Every",
    "ordinary command - `ls`, `grep`, the test suite - matches no rule and",
    "prompts. Twenty prompts per feature is not twenty decisions, it is one",
    "reflex, and the reflex is Yes. That reflex is still armed when the",
    "twenty-first prompt is the migration. Approval fatigue is the failure this",
    "tier prevents, and it is the same argument guard-protected-paths.sh makes",
    "about not firing on every source file.",
    "",
    "WHAT EARNS AN ALLOW ENTRY. All four, or it stays out:",
    "  1. It cannot write outside the working tree or the build output.",
    "  2. It cannot fetch and execute remote code.",
    "  3. It does not take an arbitrary command as an argument. This is why",
    "     `env`, `xargs`, `npx`, `watch`, `sudo`, `awk` and `sed` are absent:",
    "     each turns one allow rule into unrestricted execution.",
    "",
    "     `python`, `node`, `ruby`, `perl` and `php` ARE present, and the",
    "     command guard draws the line inside them instead: inline code",
    "     (`python3 -c …`, `node -e …`) asks, running a script file does not.",
    "     The guard cannot read either one - Python is not shell - so the",
    "     difference is what the PROMPT shows. Inline code is in the prompt and",
    "     can be judged. `python3 scripts/fix_imports.py` shows a filename, and",
    "     nobody opens the file at prompt fifteen; that prompt is a rubber",
    "     stamp, and a rubber stamp is worse than no prompt because it is what",
    "     trains the reflex. A shell payload is different again - `bash -c '…'`",
    "     IS shell, so the guard re-classifies it and denies `bash -c 'git",
    "     push --force'` outright.",
    "",
    "     `npm run`, `make` and `rake` are present on the same reasoning: the",
    "     scripts they run are repository content a human already reviews.",
    "  4. Precedence is deny -> ask -> allow, so nothing here widens a rule",
    "     above it - and both guards run BEFORE the permission system, so a",
    "     guard `deny` or `ask` still fires on a command this tier allows.",
    "     `rake db:migrate` and `npm run migrate` are denied by the guard",
    "     despite `rake:*` and `npm run:*` appearing below.",
    "",
    "WHAT LEFT THE ask TIER, AND WHY IT IS NOT A WEAKENING.",
    "`git branch`, `git worktree`, `gh api`, `glab api` and `docker exec` were",
    "ask rules. Each names an operation that READS by default and writes only",
    "when asked, and a prefix rule cannot tell the two apart - so `git branch",
    "-a`, a plain `gh api` GET and `docker exec api <test command>` each cost an",
    "approval. The command guard can tell them apart, and now does: it asks for",
    "`git branch -d`, for `gh api -X DELETE`, for `docker compose down -v` and",
    "for a shell opened inside a container, and stays silent for the read. The",
    "check moved to the layer that can make it rather than being deleted.",
    "",
    "The trade is real and worth stating: a rule here cannot fail, and a hook",
    "can. `kubectl exec` and the database clients therefore KEEP their ask",
    "rules - a cluster or a live database session can be production, and that",
    "is the wrong place to depend on a hook running.",
    "",
    "This tier is a floor, not a ceiling. Add your repository's own dev loop -",
    "its test runner, its type check, its generators - to your own",
    "settings.json. No generic list can know that `node tests/validate.mjs` is",
    "a particular repository's test suite.",
    "",
    "ALLOW RULES USE THE `verb:*` PREFIX FORM, NOT `verb *`.",
    "`Bash(git status *)` requires a space and an argument after `status`, so",
    "bare `git status` did not match the rule that existed to allow it. The",
    "deny and ask tiers keep the `verb *` form: the command guard matches those",
    "operations too, in more forms than any prefix rule can express, so their",
    "shape is settled and changing it would move fixtures for no gain.",
    "",
    "WHY defaultMode IS acceptEdits.",
    "This framework gates on the human-invoked design, approve, review and",
    "validate steps, where a person reads a plan and a diff. A per-file Edit",
    "prompt is not one of those gates: it arrives with no plan and no diff",
    "attached, and a single authorization change legitimately touches thirty",
    "files. The protected-path guard still asks for migrations, CI workflows,",
    "infrastructure definitions, lockfiles and environment files, and the deny",
    "rules below still cover secrets and keys. Remove this key if your",
    "repository wants the per-edit prompt back.",
    "",
    "Every Bash rule is mirrored as a PowerShell rule. The PowerShell tool is",
    "enabled by default on Windows without Git Bash and Bash(...) rules do not",
    "govern it, so an unmirrored floor silently disappears on those machines.",
    "",
    "File rules are only consulted for the Read and Edit tools. A Write(...),",
    "Glob(...), MultiEdit(...) or NotebookEdit(...) path rule is accepted,",
    "never consulted, and warns at startup - the worst failure shape available,",
    "because the file reads as protected. Use Read(...) and Edit(...).",
    "",
    "EVERY Read deny below has a matching Edit deny. A Read rule also blocks",
    "the Edit tool from v2.1.208, but Write and NotebookEdit are never covered",
    "by it - so the Edit rule is what actually stops every editing tool, on",
    "every version. Four paths were missing theirs and were writable.",
    "",
    "Precedence is deny -> ask -> allow, first match wins, and a deny rule",
    "cannot carry an exception. Rules here override any allow rule a developer",
    "adds in their own settings.local.json.",
    "",
    "WHAT THESE RULES DO NOT SEE: a Bash rule matches a command PREFIX, so it",
    "is blind to the same operation written any other way - a flag before the",
    "verb (git -C /elsewhere commit), an environment runner (dotenv -- ...), a",
    "quoted subcommand (git 'commit'), or an interpreter given a string",
    "(bash -c '...'). The plugin's command guard hook closes most of that gap",
    "and is documented as defence in depth, not a sandbox. For a real",
    "boundary, use OS-level sandboxing or a container."
  ],
